The SSC registry shipped in files/usr/share/qcom/sc8280xp/HUAWEI/gaokun3/sensors
comes from the Windows installation of this machine model, not from
linux-firmware. It holds the sensor definitions (config/) and the packaged
registry (registry/) that Qualcomm's Snapdragon Sensor Core needs to
enumerate and run the SH3001 accelerometer.

persist/registry/ is shipped empty on purpose: the framework needs it to
exist so it can map its writable registry there, but nothing the sensors
behind iio-sensor-proxy need is stored in it, and the DSP does not recreate
the factory calibration that used to live there.

It is redistributed the same way the vendor firmware under firmware/ is, for
the same machine only; no separate license text is available from the vendor.
